OVERVIEW

--------

This update fixes a critical signal-inversion bug in the original

release (v1.00) of EMA_Crossover_EA.mq5. Because static arrays in MQL5

are indexed chronologically rather than in series order, the initial

crossover check was triggering BUY entries on bearish crossovers

instead of bullish ones.





SUMMARY OF CHANGES (v1.01)

--------------------------



1. Fixed Inverted Bullish EMA Crossover Logic

   - In MQL5, static arrays (double fast[2], slow[2]) default to

     non-series order (oldest to newest) when populated by CopyBuffer().

     Calling CopyBuffer(handle, 0, 1, 2, array) stores the older

     completed bar (shift 2) at index 0 and the most recent completed

     bar (shift 1) at index 1.

   - Previously, UpdateCrossoverState() evaluated:

       (fast[1] <= slow[1]) && (fast[0] > slow[0])

     which checked whether the fast EMA crossed BELOW the slow EMA

     (a bearish crossover).

   - Updated the condition in UpdateCrossoverState() to:

       (fast[0] <= slow[0]) && (fast[1] > slow[1])

     so the EA properly detects a bullish crossover (fast EMA at or

     below slow EMA on the prior completed candle, and above slow EMA

     on the latest completed candle).





